WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
"Mild the mist upon the
hill," A summer evening,

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.150
after a whole day of rain.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.410
Blue mist on the mountains.

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.180
Damp in the long, green grass.

5
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.040
A faint, dreamy scent in the air.

6
00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:17.270
Far off, an old doorway glows.

7
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.350
A small figure appears, then fades.

8
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.280
She's out on a hillside.

9
00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.440
So why does the evening
take her back home?

10
00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.900
In this mission, you'll meet Emily Brontë,

11
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:33.560
who grew up at Haworth parsonage,
and dated this poem July 1839.

12
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:37.110
You'll find the exact line
where she slips back in time.

13
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.660
And you'll follow the
evening into stanzas 3 and 4.

14
00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.610
What is it doing to her?

15
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.190
Your mission: explain why
they take her back home.
